        "modules.orderLabel": "Ordering",
        "modules.orderHtml": `<ul class="checklist"><li><code>imports</code> are bootstrapped first, in container iteration order.</li><li><code>providers</code> create a new injector whose parent is the previously active injector, so earlier imported providers stay visible unless a later identifier shadows them.</li><li><code>controllers</code> are scanned only after the injector is ready.</li><li><code>bootstrap</code> runs last; keyed class names are resolved through the injector, while existing objects are kept as-is.</li></ul>`,
        "modules.diLabel": "Dependency injection boundary",
        "modules.diHtml": String.raw`<ul class="checklist"><li><code>HttpModule</code> registers <code>Router::class</code>.</li><li>Controllers are invoked through <code>PHPInjector\DI\Injector::inject()</code>.</li><li>Constructor dependencies can come from the current module or any imported module/provider chain.</li><li>Only controller classes/objects become routes; providers by themselves do not expose HTTP endpoints.</li></ul>`,
