        "operations.envLabel": "Environment variables",
        "operations.envHtml": `<ul class="checklist"><li><code>SERVER_ADDRESS</code>: defaults to <code>0.0.0.0</code> in <code>Example/index.php</code>.</li><li><code>SERVER_PORT</code>: defaults to <code>8000</code> and is published by both container workflows.</li><li><code>ENVIRONMENT</code>, <code>APP_PATH</code>, and <code>DOCKER_IMAGE_TAG</code> configure the target, application path, and image label.</li></ul>`,
        "operations.envSetupText": "Create a local .env at the repository root before either container command. These values select development, not production deployment. Compose forwards .env to the container; the Podman helpers only set selected variables and do not forward XDEBUG_MODE from that file.",
        "operations.deployLabel": "Deployment guidance",
        "operations.deployHtml": `<ul class="checklist"><li>Use <code>php Example/index.php</code> or your own front controller for direct local runs.</li><li>Because the runtime is single-process and blocking, scale by running multiple container or process instances behind a reverse proxy or platform load balancer.</li><li>The repository Docker image uses PHP <code>8.5.12</code>; the package requires PHP <code>~8.4.27 || ^8.5.12</code>.</li><li>Do not expect long-running concurrent workloads to be multiplexed inside one BraidPHP listener process.</li></ul>`,
